 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Current finding — rectangular rooms do not identify geodesic distance
+
+Bounded protected-Racket replay against generator source SHA-256
+`65a7acb082b6a340687436833d2d2789dc55005f6430a70ddda054878fb34c22`
+confirms a teaching-support gap. Replacing within-room shortest-path distance
+with Manhattan distance, while retaining room membership and lower-color tie
+breaking, fits three generated demonstrations (seeds 71/72/73, indices 0/1/2).
+It differs at two cells of an authored 5x5 nonrectangular connected-room query
+accepted by the current `self_check`. The sampler only constructs rectangular
+rooms, where those two distance rules coincide. Existing canonical examples
+include nonrectangular connected rooms, so this is relevant input topology.
+
+Evidence: packet `WORK/checks/78c2e20ad0f8/probe.py` and `result.json`, containing
+both exact Racket programs, protected runtime identity, source hashes, inputs,
+labels, and changed cells. From packet root, replay with
+`WORK/.venv/bin/python review.py run python3 ../checks/78c2e20ad0f8/probe.py`.
+
+Status: unresolved sampling/teaching-support finding; no generator or authority
+change. The distinguishing query is authored, not generated. This does not
+establish a mislabeled generated input or a failed existing generated episode.
+A future targeted repair should add a connected bent-corridor witness that
+distinguishes within-room geodesic distance from Manhattan distance.
