 Source SHA-256: `8d49b1a81531cd0d81d545fe4966af281296f9fe3c58c187e08bc076c3646f3b`.
+
+### Bounded follow-up: omitted length-four rival
+
+A separate protected-Racket probe confirmed one additional teaching gap at the
+same source hash. Four ordinary draws at seed `0`, sample indices `0,1,2,3`,
+admit a query rotation with demonstrations `0,1,3` and query `2`. The demos have
+no horizontal length-four run. A nearby rival that recolors the second cell of
+maximal horizontal runs of length **three or four**, leaving other lengths
+unchanged, matches all three Racket-labeled demos but changes query cell `(4,5)`
+from `3` to `8`. All four inputs pass `self_check`; `lesson_identifiable` returns
+`[]`, and the demos refute all three declared rivals. Thus this is an omitted
+competitor under a bounded ordinary query rotation, not a labeling failure or
+a contradiction of the existing declaration-limited claims. The existing
+side-border orientation audit is a distinct prior finding.
+
+Replay from the outer packet root:
+`python3 review.py run ../.venv/bin/python ../checks/7e7614405852/probe.py`.
+The executable probe and full source-bound result are
+`WORK/checks/7e7614405852/probe.py` and `result.json`. Eight protected Racket
+evaluations checked canonical and rival outputs on all four inputs. Only seed
+`0` was needed; no prevalence estimate, full battery, or exhaustive alternative
+search is claimed. A focused follow-up would register this rival and require a
+length-four negative example when a query contains such a run.
 
 # Decisions for 7e7614405852
 
